 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-019\", \"clauses\": {\"compare\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"Compare the numbers: {a} ___ {b}. Which sign is correct: >, <, or =?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 is a question_text family whose slots a and b print observed values across 1 to 20 (a runs 1 to 6, 8 to 12, 14 to 15, 17 to 20; b runs 1 to 20). The template asks the learner to compare the two numbers and choose the sign, which is the task named by the clause.\"}, \"two_numbers\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"Compare the numbers: {a} ___ {b}. Which sign is correct: >, <, or =?\", \"reasoning\": \"F16 places two generated numbers, a and b, in the question. Each is a separate number, so the object of the comparison is two numbers.\"}, \"up_to_20\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F16\", \"template\": \"Compare the numbers: {a} ___ {b}. Which sign is correct: >, <, or =?\", \"reasoning\": \"The printed runs for F16 reach 20 in both slots (a up to 20, b 1 to 20), and the declared bound for compare_pair is 1 to 20, so the family produces problems within the range clause.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F06\", \"F20\", \"F21\", \"F23\", \"F24\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"{actor} has {a} {a_word}. {friend} has {b} {b_word}. Which statement is true?\", \"{q} The answer is {v}.\", \"{statement}. True or False?\", \"{actor} is thinking of a number of {objects} that is greater than {a} but less than {b}. What is the number?\", \"{actor} has {a} {objects}. Another classmate has {b} {objects}. Which comparison is correct: {a} ___ {b}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F06: slot a prints a count (observed 1 to 3, 8 to 11, 13 to 16, 19 to 20) and slot a_word draws from the item list 'marble', 'marbles', 'pencil', 'pencils', 'seashell', 'seashells' with no agreement to a. Its distinct_in_every_render is false and the packet shows no rule linking the word to the count, so a count of 1 can print a plur